(5847505, 849700, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that the shot feels a little flat and the bottle draws my eye more than the fruit.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> this is ok but there are a couple of areas where you could improve. The overall feel is that the lighting is a bit flat and some more contrast would help. The composition is slightly off as the bottle is such a major element in the shot - it is a little bit crooked and feels cramped in the frame - a crop with the top of the bottle out of frame would have reduced it''s impact somewhat. There is good separation from the background.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> this is fine. For a still life challenge it is hard to do a lot more than you have here. The choice of cloth as a background works well.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> I find the shot pleasing but nothing special. The score it received is about where I''d put it.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that the shot feels a little flat and the bottle draws my eye more than the fruit. Technically this is ok but there are a couple of areas where you could improve. The overall feel is that the lighting is a bit flat and some more contrast would help. The composition is slightly off as the bottle is such a major element in the shot - it is a little bit crooked and feels cramped in the frame - a crop with the top of the bottle out of frame would have reduced it''s impact somewhat. There is good separation from the background. Artistically this is fine. For a still life challenge it is hard to do a lot more than you have here. The choice of cloth as a background works well. In summary I find the shot pleasing but nothing special. The score it received is about where I''d put it. Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 13:23:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5847523, 848192, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that this is a very good shot of a pear. The crop makes this very big and it stands out.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> This is good but there are a couple of areas that could be improved. The apple on the left is quite prominent even though blurred due to the stalk, removing the stalk would have softened it''s impact. The DOF is quite shallow and that means the stalk of the pear is OOF and we are thus left with more of a study of texture of the pear than a still life. The centred composition works quite well.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> this is not so strong. It''s a pear sitting on some apples and that''s about it. I think this is what hurt your score more than anything.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> this is an ok shot of a pear but lacks the special something to make the voter think it is anything more than that.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-02-01 13:52:19.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that this is a very good shot of a pear. The crop makes this very big and it stands out. Technically This is good but there are a couple of areas that could be improved. The apple on the left is quite prominent even though blurred due to the stalk, removing the stalk would have softened it''s impact. The DOF is quite shallow and that means the stalk of the pear is OOF and we are thus left with more of a study of texture of the pear than a still life. The centred composition works quite well. Artistically this is not so strong. It''s a pear sitting on some apples and that''s about it. I think this is what hurt your score more than anything. In summary this is an ok shot of a pear but lacks the special something to make the voter think it is anything more than that. Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 13:28:23.000000', '2010-02-01 13:52:19.000000', 0),
(5847534, 848971, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that the colours are off. It feels too bright and also a bit confusing.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> it seems like the saturation is too high or the HDR tone mapping has gone haywire! Composition is poor as there are orange bits scattered throughout the frame rather than being in an area where our eyes can settle. There are no leading lines to guide us around the placement you have chosen.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> some of the orange pieces look tatty. This couples with the haphazard approach to their placement makes this look like you just threw them down rather than thinking about what a viewer may enjoy.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> this shot falls down on both technical and artistic elements and the score reflects that.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-02-01 13:52:03.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that the colours are off. It feels too bright and also a bit confusing. Technically it seems like the saturation is too high or the HDR tone mapping has gone haywire! Composition is poor as there are orange bits scattered throughout the frame rather than being in an area where our eyes can settle. There are no leading lines to guide us around the placement you have chosen. Artistically some of the orange pieces look tatty. This couples with the haphazard approach to their placement makes this look like you just threw them down rather than thinking about what a viewer may enjoy. In summary this shot falls down on both technical and artistic elements and the score reflects that. Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 13:32:26.000000', '2010-02-01 13:52:03.000000', 0),
(5847545, 849502, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that the oranges together with the circles reducing in to the orange make a pleasing shot.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> this is good. I''d have preferred the crop to be either wider such that the plates aren''t crammed in so much or tighter so that the large plate is not fully visible. As it is there is a slight feeling of claustrophobia. I will say that the lighting does seem a bit harsh.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> this is good but you know that this works well from your PB shot. I wonder if these are the same plates with a hue change?<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> this is a good shot but the top 10 placing tells you that. Good work.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-02-01 13:51:50.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that the oranges together with the circles reducing in to the orange make a pleasing shot. Technically this is good. I''d have preferred the crop to be either wider such that the plates aren''t crammed in so much or tighter so that the large plate is not fully visible. As it is there is a slight feeling of claustrophobia. I will say that the lighting does seem a bit harsh. Artistically this is good but you know that this works well from your PB shot. I wonder if these are the same plates with a hue change? In summary this is a good shot but the top 10 placing tells you that. Good work. Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 13:36:00.000000', '2010-02-01 13:51:50.000000', 0),
(5847556, 849548, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that this is a good sharp shot with an interesting choice of items.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> this is good. The lighting is good, if a little harsh. It would have been better if it could have been focused more on the tray and less on the whole image. I''m not sure if he bottle in not vertical or if the stripes in the background cause me to think that? <br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> this is ok. It is a nice combination of items. The background is not a good choice as the stripes tend to stand out against the items a lot. A bit more blur on it would have helped, or less light.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> this is a good shot and it earned a respectable score. For only your second challenge you should be pleased.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-02-01 13:51:37.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that this is a good sharp shot with an interesting choice of items. Technically this is good. The lighting is good, if a little harsh. It would have been better if it could have been focused more on the tray and less on the whole image. I''m not sure if he bottle in not vertical or if the stripes in the background cause me to think that?  Artistically this is ok. It is a nice combination of items. The background is not a good choice as the stripes tend to stand out against the items a lot. A bit more blur on it would have helped, or less light. In summary this is a good shot and it earned a respectable score. For only your second challenge you should be pleased. Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 13:40:34.000000', '2010-02-01 13:51:37.000000', 0),
(5847560, 849644, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that the lighting is too harsh and the subject very complicated.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> the lighting seems to be the biggest issue. Is it flash lighting? There is nice separation from the background but it is very harsh indeed. The colours are also a little muted.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> the fruit is arranged in an awkward manner that means we struggle to focus on anything in particular.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> this has great potential but comes across as more of a snapshot, something DPC voters tend to frown upon.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-02-01 13:51:23.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that the lighting is too harsh and the subject very complicated. Technically the lighting seems to be the biggest issue. Is it flash lighting? There is nice separation from the background but it is very harsh indeed. The colours are also a little muted. Artistically the fruit is arranged in an awkward manner that means we struggle to focus on anything in particular. In summary this has great potential but comes across as more of a snapshot, something DPC voters tend to frown upon. Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 13:44:03.000000', '2010-02-01 13:51:23.000000', 0),
(5847568, 849023, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that processing is what this shot is about, rather than the shot itself.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> the processing is poor. Some may like the cartoon style photomatix can produce and in some cases it works but for a still life with fruit, I don''t think so. If it weren''t for this processing you would have a much higher score as the composition is good and the lighting seems fine.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> placement of the fruit is good and the candles are a really nice addition. The background could be blurred some more to enhance the separation. The border is too much I feel, it''s always best to go for less when adding borders for DPC shots.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> this could have been a great shot but the use of your processing technique cost you a full point. Even so, a new PB can''t be bad can it? ;)<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-02-01 13:51:01.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that processing is what this shot is about, rather than the shot itself. Technically the processing is poor. Some may like the cartoon style photomatix can produce and in some cases it works but for a still life with fruit, I don''t think so. If it weren''t for this processing you would have a much higher score as the composition is good and the lighting seems fine. Artistically placement of the fruit is good and the candles are a really nice addition. The background could be blurred some more to enhance the separation. The border is too much I feel, it''s always best to go for less when adding borders for DPC shots. In summary this could have been a great shot but the use of your processing technique cost you a full point. Even so, a new PB can''t be bad can it? ;) Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 13:48:38.000000', '2010-02-01 13:51:01.000000', 0),
(5847583, 849396, 63244, '<td valign="top">Fantastic image and well deserving of top honors!! This is what I need for my dining room! Congrats!</td>', 'Fantastic image and well deserving of top honors!! This is what I need for my dining room! Congrats!', '2010-02-01 13:52:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5847585, 849551, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that there is far too much going on in this shot.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> the lighting is too harsh - that will be the flash. Did you bounce it or diffuse it? Composition needs work too - the platter thing is too cramped against the edge of the frame.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> the choice of platter may not have been best but I don''t think that''s the biggest issue here. The surface you have used is too reflective and that complicates the image rather than allowing us to focus on the fruit and the bowl.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> this is a good idea but it just hasn''t come off. Try to reduce the harshness of the lighting and make the composition less complex.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM <br/> <br/>me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that there is far too much going on in this shot. Technically the lighting is too harsh - that will be the flash. Did you bounce it or diffuse it? Composition needs work too - the platter thing is too cramped against the edge of the frame. Artistically the choice of platter may not have been best but I don''t think that''s the biggest issue here. The surface you have used is too reflective and that complicates the image rather than allowing us to focus on the fruit and the bowl. In summary this is a good idea but it just hasn''t come off. Try to reduce the harshness of the lighting and make the composition less complex. Feel free to PM  me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 13:56:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5847588, 849517, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that this has a nice minimalist feel to it and that is good.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> the composition is good and the lighting is fine, if not just a little bit flat.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> there are two things I think let this shot down. First, what are those things on the apple stalk? They don''t add value and take away from the uncomplicated feel this shot has. Also, the grey background seems to be too bland, a different colour (not too colourful) or a slight pattern perhaps?<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> this shot is ok and has great potential but just doesn''t pull it off.<br/> <br/><b>PS</b>: Get out there and cast some votes ;)<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM <br/> <br/>me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that this has a nice minimalist feel to it and that is good. Technically the composition is good and the lighting is fine, if not just a little bit flat. Artistically there are two things I think let this shot down. First, what are those things on the apple stalk? They don''t add value and take away from the uncomplicated feel this shot has. Also, the grey background seems to be too bland, a different colour (not too colourful) or a slight pattern perhaps? In summary this shot is ok and has great potential but just doesn''t pull it off. PS: Get out there and cast some votes ;) Feel free to PM  me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 13:59:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5847592, 849581, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that the shot is nice and crisp with some intrigue. Once I view for longer I start to see the issues.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> the composition is good but it''s those dot things that balance the shot. The pears are a little too close to the left edge. The lighting is good in that is has the pears against a crisp white background but this is a double-edged sword in that it also makes the shot seem a bit sterile.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> those dot things confuse us viewers. How do they relate to the fruit? Is this an "artistic" element?<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> this has some really good points but I think the average voters was confused by those dots and the sterile feel.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM <br/> <br/>me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that the shot is nice and crisp with some intrigue. Once I view for longer I start to see the issues. Technically the composition is good but it''s those dot things that balance the shot. The pears are a little too close to the left edge. The lighting is good in that is has the pears against a crisp white background but this is a double-edged sword in that it also makes the shot seem a bit sterile. Artistically those dot things confuse us viewers. How do they relate to the fruit? Is this an "artistic" element? In summary this has some really good points but I think the average voters was confused by those dots and the sterile feel. Feel free to PM  me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 14:03:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5847597, 848862, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that the shot is good as it is nicely balanced and the fruit is arranged so as to help the flow of our eye.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> the lighting seems a bit harsh (see the hotspots on the fruit) and it is concentrated in an area that is a little too small as it drops off on some of the fruit too soon for my liking. The DOF is large enough but that banana seems a little soft to me.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> I like the choice of background but the widescreen style framing is not a good look here. Often it helps a crop like this but there I think it is too much of a contrast with the shot itself and with a fruit still life, a dramatic contrast is not what is needed.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> this is a good shot that has a couple of areas for improvement that held it back.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM <br/> <br/>me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that the shot is good as it is nicely balanced and the fruit is arranged so as to help the flow of our eye. Technically the lighting seems a bit harsh (see the hotspots on the fruit) and it is concentrated in an area that is a little too small as it drops off on some of the fruit too soon for my liking. The DOF is large enough but that banana seems a little soft to me. Artistically I like the choice of background but the widescreen style framing is not a good look here. Often it helps a crop like this but there I think it is too much of a contrast with the shot itself and with a fruit still life, a dramatic contrast is not what is needed. In summary this is a good shot that has a couple of areas for improvement that held it back. Feel free to PM  me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-01 14:07:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5847605, 848104, 30214, '<td valign="top">nice composition with great colors, Lydia!<br/> <br/>eta: the glass bottles in the back look flat and distorted. I don''t know how you achieved this look , but I like it a lot, they actually seem like something out of post-imressionism era than "old masters"<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-02-01 14:21:10.</i></td>', 'nice composition with great colors, Lydia! eta: the glass bottles in the back look flat and distorted. I don''t know how you achieved this look , but I like it a lot, they actually seem like something out of post-imressionism era than "old masters"', '2010-02-01 14:17:19.000000', '2010-02-01 14:21:10.000000', 0),
